Touchless Door Bell Using IR Sensor – Project Report

Introduction

A touchless doorbell is an electronic system that allows a person to ring a bell without physically pressing a switch. This project uses an IR (Infrared) sensor to detect the presence of a hand near the sensor. When the hand is detected, the sensor sends a signal to activate a buzzer or bell.
This system is useful for maintaining hygiene and reducing the spread of germs because no physical contact is required. It is commonly used in homes, hospitals, offices, and public places.


Objective of the Project

To design a touch-free doorbell system using an IR sensor.
To reduce physical contact with doorbell switches.
To understand the working of IR sensors and electronic circuits.
To build a simple, low-cost, and efficient automation project.


