Basic Connections

-Connect VCC of IR sensor to +5V supply.
-Connect GND of IR sensor to ground.
-Connect OUT pin of IR sensor to the base of transistor through a resistor.
-Connect buzzer to collector terminal of transistor.
Emitter terminal is connected to ground.
-Power the circuit using a battery or adapter.


Working Principle

•The IR sensor consists of an IR transmitter and an IR receiver.
•The IR transmitter continuously emits infrared rays.
•When a hand comes near the sensor, the IR rays reflect back.
•The IR receiver detects the reflected rays.
•The sensor output becomes HIGH.
•The transistor gets activated and allows current to flow.
•The buzzer rings like a doorbell.
